n Note","author":"T. Nguyen, RN","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:21","category":"Nursing Note","summary":"Admission database and baseline assessment completed.","body":"**Admission assessment**\n- Arrived to the unit at 0645 from the ED. ID band and allergy band verified (No known drug allergies.).\n- Vitals on arrival: T 100.2 F, HR 88, BP 123/73, RR 16, SpO2 97% on room air, pain 4/10.\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Left forearm: red, warm, tender area about 7 x 5 cm, border outlined; no drainage.\n- Pain 4/10; left forearm, aching, 4/10.\n- Skin: Left forearm: red, warm, tender area about 7 x 5 cm, border outlined; no drainage. Braden 21.\n- Fall risk: Moderate; fall precautions in place.\n- Lines: none.\n\n**Education**\n- Oriented to room, call light, plan of care, and fall precautions.\n\n**Plan**"},{"id":"note_hospitalist_history_and_physical_2026_10_20_07_15","type":"hp","title":"Hospitalist History and Physical","author":"S. Patel, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:15","category":"H&P","summary":"Admission H&P for cellulitis of the left forearm with nausea.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Red, painful left forearm and nausea\n\n**History of present illness**\n63-year-old male with type 2 diabetes and a red, warm, tender left forearm for 2 days after an insect bite. Low-grade fever and nausea at home. No pus. Admitted for an oral antibiotic, an antinausea injection and sliding-scale insulin.\n\n**Past medical history**\n- No significant past medical history.\n\n**Past surgical history**\n- No prior surgeries.\n\n**Home medications**\n- None\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Family history**\n- Mother with hypertension; father with coronary artery disease. No known family history of bowel disease or cancer.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Review of systems**\n- Positive for arm redness, warmth, pain, nausea and a low-grade fever. Negative for vomiting, chest pain, shortness of breath and diarrhea.\n\n**Vitals**\n- T 100.2 F, HR 88, BP 123/73, RR 16, SpO2 97% on room air, pain 4/10 | Wt 84 kg, BMI 28.4\n\n**Physical exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Left forearm: red, warm, tender area about 7 x 5 cm, border outlined; no drainage.\n\n**Data**\n- Labs: \n\n**Assessment and plan**\n63-year-old male with no significant history admitted with cellulitis of the left forearm with nausea.\n\n**Cellulitis of the left forearm with nausea**\n\n**Prophylaxis / code status**\n- DVT prophylaxis per orders; fall precautions.\n- Code status: Full Code."},{"id":"note_ed_provider_note_2026_10_20_06_03","type":"erVisitSummary","title":"ED Provider Note","author":"J. Whitaker, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 06:03","category":"ED Note","summary":"63-year-old male presenting with red, painful left forearm and nausea; admitted to Hospital Medicine.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Red, painful left forearm and nausea\n\n**HPI**\n63-year-old male with type 2 diabetes and a red, warm, tender left forearm for 2 days after an insect bite. Low-grade fever and nausea at home. No pus. Admitted for an oral antibiotic, an antinausea injection and sliding-scale insulin.\n\n**Past medical / surgical history**\n- Medical: No significant past medical history.\n- Surgical: No prior surgeries.\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Triage vitals**\n- T 100.2 F, HR 90, BP 121/77, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 5/10\n\n**Exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Left forearm: red, warm, tender area about 7 x 5 cm, border outlined; no drainage.\n\n**ED results**\n- Labs: pending\n\n**ED course**\n- 0445 cephalexin (KEFLEX) capsule 250 mg Oral\n- 0445 insulin lispro (HUMALOG) Per moderate-dose sliding scale Subcutaneous\n- 0445 promethazine (PHENERGAN) 12.5 mg Intramuscular\n\n**Assessment / disposition**\n- Cellulitis of the left forearm with nausea. \n- Admit to Hospital Medicine (Dr. S. Patel); condition guarded but stable."}],"timeline":{"marDate":"Tuesday, October 20, 2026","marTimeSlots":["0800","0900","1000","1100","1200","1300","1400","1500"],"simulationStart":"2026-10-20 08:45","simulationEnd":"2026-10-20 16:45"},"simulationTasks":[],"triggers":[],"facultyBuilder":{"builderVersion":2,"inputs":{"name":"Raymond Cho","age":63,"sex":"Male","mrn":"SIM-30418","unit":"Medical-Surgical 2 East","room":"218-1","heightCm":172,"weightKg":84,"primary":"lpn_cephalexin","hospitalDay":1,"simDate":"2026-10-20","startTime":"08:45","hx":[],"surg":[],"surgText":"","allergies":[],"codeStatus":"Full Code","social":{"tobacco":"Never","alcohol":"None","drugs":"None","living":"Lives with spouse/partner","function":"Independent","other":""},"studentLevel":"First-semester LPN","complexity":"simple","facultyNotes":"","id":"lpn_cephalexin","desc":"PO cephalexin 250 mg, SubQ insulin lispro (moderate scale, glucose 280 = 9 units), IM promethazine (Phenergan) 12.5 mg = 0.5 mL"}}}}